    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Lawrence Butler**, whose score of 73.47 makes him our primary offensive engine. He benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Chris Bassitt, who sits at a 4.36 xERA. Close behind is **Taylor Ward** (69.99), who also exploits the friendly park environment against Luis Severino. While the platoon advantage for **Taylor Ward** is slightly negative, his raw output remains strong enough to secure a top-tier slot. **Bryson Stott** (68.39) rounds out our strongest performers; despite the projected #9 hole, he earns significant value from a 13% platoon edge and a soft matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano, whose 4.73 xERA is a primary driver for **Bryson Stott**\u2019s efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision was the final bench spot, where **Geraldo Perdomo** (54.66) narrowly missed the cut. While **Geraldo Perdomo** provides the elite sprint speed we covet for our stolen base targets, he was ultimately nudged out by the combined stability of **Wenceel Perez** (60.67) and **Masyn Winn** (59.98). **Masyn Winn** specifically holds value today due to his 90% steal probability against the slow delivery of Walker Buehler, which keeps him ahead of the bench despite a tougher opposing arm. **Daulton Varsho** remains a start despite the marginal score of 56.88 and the 1% penalty for an elite opposing catcher, as his specific profile provides necessary diversification in our 5x5 build.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, as the absence of official confirmation introduces variance into our projected batting order points\u2014particularly for **Will Smith**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Brendan Donovan**. While **Brendan Donovan** enjoys a massive 10% boost for an assumed leadoff role, any shift down the order will recalibrate his expected efficiency. Similarly, we are monitoring the risk associated with **Jung Hoo Lee**, whose 54.81 score is relatively thin; should he be removed from the top of the order against Bubba Chandler, we may see a further dip in his daily utility. Keep a close watch on weather reports, as the park-heavy projections for **Taylor Ward**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Lawrence Butler** are sensitive to any shifting winds.",
